    "summary": "High‑energy Fox Theatre set with soaring The Other One and epic NFA finale",
    "blurb": "The show builds from a relaxed opening into powerful jams, highlighted by a smoking The Other One and an explosive Not Fade Away > Greatest Story Ever Told > Not Fade Away sequence. Keith’s inspired solo in The Other One and Bill’s tight drum work add extra sparkle. Soundboard capture is clear enough to enjoy every nuance of the band’s high‑energy flow.",
    "review": "October 19, 1972 at St. Louis’ Fox Theatre finds the Dead riding a wave of momentum that starts mellow and surges into pure electric bliss. After a concise first set that includes tight renditions of Jack Straw, Sugaree and the classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, the second set launches with Bird Song before diving into a Truckin' → Drums → The Other One suite that showcases Bill Kreutzmann’s rolling fills and Keith Godchaux’s rare, soaring solo. The momentum carries through a blistering He's Gone and returns to The Other One for an extended jam that feels both exploratory and cohesive. The night caps off with a masterful Not Fade Away > Greatest Story Ever Told > Not Fade Away sandwich and a heartfelt Comes A Time, leaving the audience buzzing as the lights come up.",
